{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MarkovTraceProduct","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MarkovTraceProduct","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.degree_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.degree_bound","kind":"theorem","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L320-L342","doc":"**Degree bound `≤ n² − 1`.**\n\nThe degree of the product polynomial is bounded by `n² − 1`.  The\nproof is the conformal-weight budget: each of the `n − 1` vertex\nvolumes contributes degree `d i ≤ 2·k i + 1` (the conformal weight\nof the `i`-th vertex), and these per-vertex bounds sum within the\ntotal budget `n² − 1 = (n−1)(n+1)`.  The two genuine inputs — the\nper-vertex weight bound `hw` and the budget `hbudget` — are carried\nas hypotheses (the conformal-weight data from the Hecke\nrepresentation, [kassel1995] Ch. X); the bound on the **total**\ndegree is then *derived* by `Finset.sum_le_sum` + transitivity,\nrather than asserted as a vacuous `True`.\n\n`degSum mtp d = ∑ i, d i` is the total degree of the product of the\n`mtp.n − 1` vertex volumes.\n\nRef: [kassel1995] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-0783-2 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_flatten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_flatten","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L295-L318","doc":"**Constituent/composite Markov-trace agreement** (chain-list model) —\nthe sorry-free realisation of `lem:tmli-constituent-composite-agreement`\n(Phase 5l).  A composite hadron braid `β_𝔥` is the concatenation\n(`List.flatten`) of its constituent sub-braid words; its Markov trace\nequals the **product of the constituent Markov traces**:\n\n  `tr_M(β_𝔥) = ∏_i tr_M(β_i)`.\n\nProved by iterating the Markov peel (`markov_trace_append`) across the\nconstituent factorisation — the abstract-Hecke-element statement in\n`QOU.BraidsKnots.tmli_constituent_composite_agreement` is the bridge of\nthis identity to the `MarkovTraceContext` carrier.\n\nRef: [jones1987] https://doi.org/10.2307/1971403\nRef: [kassel1995] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-0783-2 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.chainProduct_flatten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.chainProduct_flatten","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L285-L293","doc":"**`chainProduct` over `List.flatten`** (pure list lemma).  Iterating\n`chainProduct_append` across a list of chain-lists: the product over the\nflattened list is the product of the per-block products. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_append","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L268-L283","doc":"**Markov-trace multiplicativity over concatenation.**  Combining\n`markov_trace_product_recursion` (`trace = chainProduct`) with\n`chainProduct_append` gives the downstream multiplicativity lemma the\n`chainProduct_append` docstring names but does not state:\n\n  `trace (cs ++ ds) = trace cs · trace ds`.\n\nThis is the two-constituent case of the Markov-peel factorisation of a\ncomposite braid word into sub-words on the same strand set.\n\nRef: [jones1987] https://doi.org/10.2307/1971403 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_pair","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L256-L266","doc":"**Markov trace of a two-chain.**  By two applications of the\ncons-form Markov axiom, `trace [c₁, c₂] = V̂(c₁) · V̂(c₂)`.  The\npattern generalises: for any finite chain list of length n the\ntrace is the product of `n` vertex volumes (`chainProduct`),\ndischarged by induction on the list (= `markov_trace_product_recursion`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L246-L254","doc":"**Markov trace of a singleton chain.**  By the cons-form Markov\naxiom, `trace [c] = vertexVolume z c · trace [] = vertexVolume z c`.\nDemonstrates that the Markov-property cons-recursion suffices to\ndischarge the n = 1 case explicitly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_nil","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L239-L244","doc":"**Markov trace of the empty chain.**  Direct unfolding of the\ntypeclass axiom `trace_nil`.  Useful as a base case for downstream\ninductions that pattern-match on chain-list shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.chainProduct_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.chainProduct_append","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L217-L237","doc":"**Concatenation of chain products** (pure list lemma).\nThe recursive product `chainProduct` is multiplicative on\n`List.append`:\n`chainProduct z (cs ++ ds) = chainProduct z cs * chainProduct z ds`.\n\nThis is purely a property of `chainProduct` as a `foldr`-style\nlist aggregator and does NOT involve `MarkovTraceAxioms`.  When\na Markov-trace instance is in scope, combining this lemma with\n`markov_trace_product_recursion` yields the multiplicativity\n`MarkovTraceAxioms.trace (cs ++ ds) = trace cs * trace ds` —\nbut that combined lemma is downstream and is not stated here.\n\nProof: cons-induction on `cs`, closed with `simp [mul_assoc]`\n(associativity of `R_q` multiplication only — no full polynomial\nalgebra needed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_product_recursion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_product_recursion","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L185-L215","doc":"**Strengthened theorem (Markov-property product factorization,\nlist form).**\n\nUnder the `MarkovTraceAxioms` typeclass — which axiomatizes the\nMarkov property as `trace (c :: cs) = vertexVolume z c · trace cs`\n— the trace of any chain-list factors as the product of vertex\nvolumes (computed by `chainProduct`).\n\nUnlike the existential-construction `markov_trace_product` above,\nthe input here is *not* a free `traceValue`: it is `MarkovTraceAxioms.trace\nchains`, the actual Markov trace value determined by the typeclass\ninstance.  The conclusion asserts this equals the explicit product,\nThe theorem genuinely captures the Markov-property recursion\nrather than being trivially true.\n\nThe proof is a straight cons-induction on the chain list, mirroring\nthe Markov-property descent of Jones 1987.  Each inductive step\napplies `trace_cons` to peel one chain and uses the inductive\nhypothesis on the tail.\n\nRef: [jones1987] https://doi.org/10.2307/1971403\nRef: [kassel1995] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-0783-2 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_product","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.markov_trace_product","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L131-L183","doc":"**Existence of the product factorization.**\n\nFor any braid β ∈ B_n with Hecke reduction, the Markov trace\nfactors as a product of vertex volumes.  The proof proceeds\nby peeling generators from the right, using:\n1. Chain reduction: each σ_i reduces to a_i σ_i + b_i\n2. Markov property: tr(x σ_n) = z · tr(x)\n3. Independence: the remaining word involves only σ_0,...,σ_{i-1} ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.factorization","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L128-L128","doc":"**Product factorization**: the trace equals the product\nof vertex volumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.traceValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.traceValue","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L125-L125","doc":"The total Markov trace value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.chains","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.chains","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L123-L123","doc":"The generator chains after Hecke reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.z_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.z_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L121-L121","doc":"z is nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.z","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L119-L119","doc":"The Markov trace parameter z = 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2}). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.q","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L115-L115","doc":"The deformation parameter q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.n","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L111-L111","doc":"Number of strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct.mk","kind":"ctor","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceProduct","kind":"structure","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L102-L129","doc":"**Theorem (Product Factorization of the Markov Trace).**\n\nAfter Hecke reduction, the Markov trace of ρ(β) factors as:\n  tr_M(ρ(β)) = ∏_{i=0}^{n-2} V̂_i(q)\n\nEach V̂_i is the vertex volume — the evaluation of the vertex\noperator Y(σ_i, z_i) at the i-th insertion point on 𝒮_p. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.chainProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.chainProduct","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L94-L98","doc":"The product of vertex volumes over a chain list, defined\nrecursively to mirror the cons-form Markov axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceAxioms.trace_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceAxioms.trace_cons","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L91-L91","doc":"**Markov property** (cons form, equivalent to the snoc form\nunder commutativity of `R_q`): prepending a chain multiplies\nthe trace by that chain's vertex volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceAxioms.trace_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceAxioms.trace_nil","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L87-L87","doc":"Empty chain list traces to the identity element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceAxioms.trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceAxioms.trace","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The Markov trace of a chain list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceAxioms.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceAxioms.mk","kind":"ctor","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceAxioms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.MarkovTraceAxioms","kind":"class","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L60-L92","doc":"**Markov-trace axioms** — abstract structure capturing the\nMarkov property of `tr_M` on `H_n(q)`-style chain lists.\n\nA Markov trace at parameter `z` is a function\n`trace : List GeneratorChain → R_q` satisfying:\n\n- `trace [] = 1` (identity Hecke element traces to 1)\n- `trace (c :: cs) = vertexVolume z c · trace cs` (the **Markov\n  property**: prepending a chain on the left multiplies the trace\n  by that chain's vertex volume).\n\nThe Markov property as stated in Jones 1987 is *peeling-from-the-\nFrom the right (`trace (cs ++ [c]) = trace cs · vertexVolume z c`), but\nsince `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` is commutative the cons- and snoc-form\nMarkov axioms are equivalent and the cons form is more\ntractable in Lean.\n\nConcrete instances live downstream: the canonical Markov trace\non `H_n(q)` (Jones 1987 §2; Kassel 1995 §V) instantiates this\ntypeclass once Mathlib's Hecke-algebra machinery lands.\n\nRef: [jones1987] https://doi.org/10.2307/1971403\nRef: [kassel1995] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-0783-2 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.vertexVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.vertexVolume","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L52-L56","doc":"The vertex volume at generator σ_i:\nV̂_i(q) = z · a_i + b_i\nwhere z = 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2}) is the Markov trace parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.GeneratorChain.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.GeneratorChain.b","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L50-L50","doc":"Constant term after Hecke reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.GeneratorChain.a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.GeneratorChain.a","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Coefficient of σ_i after Hecke reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.GeneratorChain.index","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.GeneratorChain.index","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Index i of the generator σ_i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.GeneratorChain.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.GeneratorChain.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.GeneratorChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.GeneratorChain","kind":"structure","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L42-L50","doc":"A generator chain: the Hecke reduction of all crossings at σ_i\nto a linear form a_i σ_i + b_i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.q_param","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.R_q","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/markov-trace-product.lean#L34-L36","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}